Phoenix RPi4: don't re-register an already-registered stipple damage.

glamor_track_stipple() is called from glamor_validate_gc() on every GCStipple
change, but the DamagePtr is created once and cached in gc_priv, so from the
second stipple change onward it called DamageRegister() on a damage that was
already the head of the drawable's damage list.

damageInsertDamage() prepends unconditionally (its "Damage already on list"
check is behind DAMAGE_VALIDATE_ENABLE, off in normal builds), so the node
self-links: pDamage->pNext == pDamage. damageRemoveDamage() then unlinks the
first match and writes *pPrev = pDamage->pNext -- i.e. pDamage again -- so the
list head still references the node after DamageDestroy() has freed it. A later
DamageUnregister() reads a recycled heap chunk as a DamagePtr and dereferences
pDamage->pDrawable->pScreen.

Observed on Pi 4 as a Data Abort (EL0) in the X desktop-exit path, every run:

  doFreeResource -> FreeGC -> glamor_destroy_gc -> glamor_invalidate_stipple
    -> DamageUnregister (damage.c:1796 damageScrPriv(pScreen))
      -> dixLookupPrivate -> dixGetPrivate  ldr x0,[x0]
  far = x0 = 0x60, x1 = 0  =>  pScreen->devPrivates == NULL,
  damageScrPrivateKeyRec.offset == 0x60
  pDamage->pDrawable = 0x3ad9c8, outside both the image (0x400000-0x1baac80)
  and the heap, with a self-pointer at +16 -- i.e. allocator metadata in a
  freed chunk, not a live drawable.

Fix: register only when the damage is not already on the drawable we want, and
move it (unregister first) if the GC's stipple pixmap changed.
--- a/glamor/glamor_core.c
+++ b/glamor/glamor_core.c
@@ -182,8 +182,31 @@
                                                    glamor_stipple_damage_destroy,
                                                    DamageReportNonEmpty,
                                                    TRUE, gc->pScreen, gc);
-        if (gc_priv->stipple_damage)
-            DamageRegister(&gc->stipple->drawable, gc_priv->stipple_damage);
+        if (gc_priv->stipple_damage) {
+            DrawablePtr stipple = &gc->stipple->drawable;
+
+            /* Register only if this damage is not already on that drawable.
+             *
+             * DamageRegister() -> damageInsertDamage() prepends
+             * unconditionally; its "Damage already on list" check is compiled
+             * out unless DAMAGE_VALIDATE_ENABLE. Re-registering a damage that
+             * is already the head of the drawable's list therefore self-links
+             * it (pNext == pDamage), and damageRemoveDamage() then leaves the
+             * head pointing at the node it just unlinked. The list keeps a
+             * dangling reference after DamageDestroy() frees the damage, so a
+             * later DamageUnregister() reads a recycled heap chunk as a
+             * DamagePtr and faults on pDamage->pDrawable->pScreen.
+             *
+             * glamor_track_stipple() is called from glamor_validate_gc() on
+             * every GCStipple change while the damage is created once and
+             * cached in gc_priv, so without this guard the second stipple
+             * change on a GC double-registers. */
+            if (gc_priv->stipple_damage->pDrawable != stipple) {
+                if (gc_priv->stipple_damage->pDrawable != NULL)
+                    DamageUnregister(gc_priv->stipple_damage);
+                DamageRegister(stipple, gc_priv->stipple_damage);
+            }
+        }
     }
 }
 
